## 5. Owner Authentication and Admin Dashboard

Implement a secure, owner-only administration system.

The website owner must be able to log in and manage portfolio projects without editing code.

### Authentication

- Create a secure login page at `/admin/login`.
- Restrict dashboard routes and protected operations to authenticated owners.
- Use secure, HTTP-only session cookies.
- Apply appropriate `Secure`, `SameSite`, and expiration settings.
- Hash passwords using a modern, secure password hashing algorithm supported by the selected authentication solution.
- Never store plaintext passwords.
- Never expose password hashes, session secrets, or authentication tokens to the client.
- Implement logout and session expiration.
- Validate all protected operations on the server, not just in the UI.
- Use environment variables for secrets and credentials.
- Do not provide public registration.
- Provide a secure initial owner-account setup process that does not require hardcoded credentials.
- Prevent unauthorized users from accessing admin APIs, uploads, or protected actions.

Do not hardcode a default administrator password into the source code or seed scripts.

