Do not trust arbitrary video embed HTML supplied by users.

### Media storage architecture

Separate media storage from portfolio metadata.

Use a media storage service or adapter so the application can support:

1. Local persistent storage for development.
2. A persistent production volume or object storage provider for deployment.

Do not store large image or video binaries directly in SQLite.

Store media metadata and storage references in SQLite.

IMPORTANT: Do not assume a local filesystem or SQLite database is persistent on serverless hosting. Explain deployment requirements clearly and support an appropriate persistent storage configuration for the chosen hosting platform.

If local uploads are used, store them outside the public source directories where possible, validate access, and serve them through a controlled, secure mechanism. Never expose private uploads simply because they exist in a public folder.

